    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10049" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conductor</span></b> , ōris, m.
		conduco, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>one who hires a thing, a lessee, farmer, tenant, a
				contractor</i> (rare, and mostly <i>absol.</i>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(histrionum),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. As. prol. 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(pecoris),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 150, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(agri),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. C. 3, 21</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Col. 3, 13, 12</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep.
				7, 30, 3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(aedificii),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 14, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">operis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Q. Fr. 3, 1, 2, § 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sacrae arae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Max. 8, 12</span></i>
			, ext. 1: <i><span class="en">Dig. 40, 7, 40, § 5</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 46</span></i>;
			<i><span class="en">4324</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Gai.
				Inst. 3, 145</span></i>.</div>
